$('help').onclick=()=>modal('Your simulation whiteboard',`<p><b>Object types:</b> Create a reusable object. Choose a basic color or upload PNG/JPEG artwork. Defaults are monochrome. Collision, movement, tags, and appearance are independent settings. Solid, liquid, and moving-object presets only set starting flags.</p><p><b>Stats:</b> Define any named number with a minimum, maximum, and starting value. There are no built-in survival bars. Values are clamped to your range.</p><p><b>Rules:</b> On interaction, contact, or each tick, read a condition and apply an effect to Self or Other. Effects can change a stat, add/remove a tag, transfer material to a surface, move surface material inside, or remove an object. Contact rules repeat each tick.</p><p><b>Build an interaction chain:</b> Create a material object type. Give it an On contact → Other → Transfer supply onto surface rule. On another object type, add an Every tick → Self → Move surface material inside rule using that material. Then add a rule comparing internal material quantity and changing any custom stat you defined. No species-specific code is needed.</p><p><b>Utility:</b> Add decisions using your stats. Score low or high values, set a weight, then choose idle, movement, or a find → move → interact branch. The highest score wins. This version uses fixed action branches; arbitrary behavior-tree node authoring is still future work.</p><p><b>Board:</b> Draw with your object types; Select to inspect an instance. Click stacked instances repeatedly to cycle them. Ctrl+Z undoes edits. Manual interaction uses the selected object and an adjacent target. Objects share cells unless both have collision.</p><p><b>Persistence:</b> Save stores definitions, instances, rules, and uploaded artwork on the backend. Export/import JSON provides portable backups. The current 64 × 44 board supports 500 instances, 100 object types, and 50 stats; projects can be up to 12 MB. Simulation runs in the open tab. Legacy v0.1 projects remain available as backups in Projects.</p>`,'QUICK GUIDE');
